// PARAM: --analysis interval
// Adapted from Goblint tests/regression/56-witness/26-mine-tutorial-ex4.6.c
// (Mine's tutorial, example 4.6): a counter runs from 40 down to 0 and
// exits on x != 0. Goblint proves the in-loop bounds only by unassuming
// a YAML witness (26-mine-tutorial-ex4.6.yml); the post-loop x == 0 needs
// no witness.
//
// Voblint proves x == 0 but neither in-loop bound. Mechanism: the head
// widens x from [40,40] against [39,40] and drops the lower bound to
// -2147483648. On that interval x - 1 may underflow, so the decrement
// yields the full i32 range and the head becomes top; the guard (x != 0)
// excludes only the single value 0, which is not a bound. x == 0 holds
// because the exit edge asserts equality. The same program under
// --analysis int (16-composite-domain/known-imprecision/
// 02-mine_ex46_decreasing_counter.vimp) loses the bounds the same way.
fun main() {
  x = 40;
  while (x != 0) {
    __voblint_check(x <= 40); // UNKNOWN
    x = x - 1;
    __voblint_check(x >= 0); // UNKNOWN
  }
  __voblint_check(x == 0); // PROVED
}
